    "intro_narrative": "You step into the dimly lit office of Arthur Pendelton, a renowned private investigator who vanished without a trace exactly three weeks ago. The air is thick with stale tobacco smoke and the sharp scent of ozone. A faint, rhythmic hum emanates from an array of strange, interconnected retro-futuristic machines covering his massive oak desk. Suddenly, the heavy steel door slams shut behind you, engaging a magnetic deadlock. A digital timer flickers to life above the exit, ticking down ominously. Arthur was known for his intense paranoia, leaving behind a trail of cryptic devices and physical puzzles to protect his final, earth-shattering discovery. You must navigate his bizarre contraptions, uncover the hidden sequence of events, and piece together the fragmented clues he left behind. Your only way out is to operate his master machinery and reveal the final truth Arthur died to hide. The clock is ticking, and the shadows of the office seem to close in around you.",
    "narrative_style": "mystery"
  },
